From: System Electronics
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:50:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm: dsi: give the enable delays their working defaults

Both delays existed but were inert, and the values are now measured.

300 ms before the first scanout after probe: without it the first modeset
of every boot ends with the generator stopped and the panel dark, with it
two boots out of two come up clean, one of them from cold. The cost is
paid once.

20 ms before VID_EN on every enable: at a pipeline exit 300 ms never
helped, 0 out of 9, so the long delay would be black screen for nothing.
20 ms is one frame plus margin.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform workaround]

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
@@ -946,7 +946,7 @@
 	dsi->link_initialized = true;
 }
 
-static unsigned int video_delay_ms;
+static unsigned int video_delay_ms = 20;
 module_param(video_delay_ms, uint, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(video_delay_ms, "Diagnostic: delay in ms before enabling video, after the lanes are ready");
 
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/hailo/hailo_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/hailo/hailo_drv.c
@@ -98,7 +98,7 @@
 	DRM_FORMAT_RGB888,
 };
 
-static unsigned int first_enable_delay_ms;
+static unsigned int first_enable_delay_ms = 300;
 module_param(first_enable_delay_ms, uint, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(first_enable_delay_ms, "Diagnostic: delay in ms before the first scanout after probe");
 
